# Normalize line endings independently of the client.
#
# The repo is edited from both WSL and Windows. Git for Windows sets
# core.autocrlf=true system-wide, WSL does not, so the two clients disagreed
# about whether files were modified. Declaring the rule here makes both write
# LF to the repository and to the working tree, whatever their global config.
#
# LF also matters for the containers: a shell script with CRLF line endings
# fails with "bad interpreter: no such file or directory".
* text=auto eol=lf
